  "verified_mechanisms": [
    "Rust owns page, pane-bar and divider rectangles for side-by-side/stacked splits, including tiny bounds and odd remainder distribution. The single page fills the host with split controls hidden.",
    "Pane titles use Rust display-list text with cached native font measurement, tight text tiles and an empty-title guard. No hidden title Labels are created; a single native group name preserves accessibility.",
    "Three clipped UI canvases draw both pane bars and the divider with the existing shared Metal device/queue/pipeline. Their screen bounds do not intersect either WebContents. Parent-relative rounded-card backing preserves outer corners.",
    "Rust owns divider pointer/gesture ratio state, clamping to 0.2..0.8, release/capture-loss commit and cancellation when the pane identity or orientation changes. Native ResizeArea remains the cursor/event/AX adapter. Horizontal RTL reversal has Rust unit coverage, not full native RTL validation.",
    "Pane menu/close and row close children use the established Rust mouse/key reducer. Existing application commands and native default accessibility actions remain; analytic More/Close GPU primitives add no external assets.",
    "Invalidations coalesce independently of native rasterization; unchanged scene fingerprints skip submissions. Native painting returns when Metal is unavailable and all split surfaces hide on unsplit/window hide.",
    "The new native case physically drags both divider axes, checks a gesture stream and cancelled stale drag, updates a Unicode title under a native paint lock, verifies page/surface non-overlap and fallback painting, and closes a real split half.",
    "The full sidebar, footer, scroll, split/folder/pin/session, workspace transition, settings, keyboard and large-sidebar regression matrix remains green."
  ],
  "manual_observations": [
    "The matching signed, timestamped app displayed both Unicode pane titles, menu/close controls and the divider without obscuring either loopback page.",
    "The actual pane menu changed side-by-side panels to stacked panels and back. Both layouts rendered correctly; the original split pair, 24 demo tabs and pinned sidebar were retained.",
    "The isolated prototype was closed and its launcher exited successfully. The normal application/profile was not used."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "Native View/Button/ResizeArea containers, event delivery, cursor, focus/AX, menu services and browser/WebContents commands remain adapters; this is not full Views removal.",
    "Sidebar resizing/autohide state, workspace animation snapshots and remaining palettes/forms/service presentation still require migration.",
    "Physical trackpad, VoiceOver, IME, native RTL and display-scale matrices remain required.",
    "Controlled real-workload CPU/GPU and actual presentation comparison remains required. Test elapsed times and submitted command buffers do not measure presentation latency or establish a performance gain.",
    "No new third-party dependency, crate or framework was introduced; original-code Apache-2.0 and required upstream notices are unchanged."
  ]
